    银牌 | yín pái | silver medal
    白银 | bái yín | silver
    金银 | jīn yín | gold and silver

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 银子 historical currency designation specifically highlighting silver ingots or colloquial hard money.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 银子 vs. 钱 | qián | 银子 refers specifically to silver currency or ancient monetary ingots, whereas 钱 is the universal contemporary term for money.
    2 | 银子 vs. 白银 | báiyín | 银子 is historical, narrative, and spoken, whereas 白银 is the formal chemical and macroeconomic commodity term.
    3 | 银子 vs. 钞票 | chāopiào | 银子 refers to metallic silver specie, whereas 钞票 strictly designates paper banknotes and printed currency.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 子路用打工换来的银子在集镇上买了一大袋上等白米。他紧紧攥着剩下的一点碎银子，心中满是欣喜，因为这些粮食足够让年迈的父母吃上几个月的饱饭了。 | Zǐlù yòng dǎgōng huànlái de yínzi zài jīzhèn shàng mǎi le yí dà dài shàngděng báimǐ. Tā jǐnjǐn zuànzhe shèngxià de yìdiǎn suìyínzi, xīnzhōng mǎn shì xīnxǐ, yīnwèi zhèxiē liángshi zúgòu ràng niánmài de fùmǔ chī shang jǐ gè yuè de bǎofàn le. | With the silver earned from his labor, Zilu bought a large sack of premium white rice at the town market. Gripping the remaining broken silver tightly, he rejoiced knowing this food would nourish his parents for months. | Con la plata ganada en su faena, Zilu compró un gran saco de arroz de primera en el pueblo. Apretando contra su pecho los pocos trozos de plata sobrantes, sintió una alegría inmensa sabiendo que sus padres no pasarían hambre en meses.
  #2 | 明清以来的经济史研究证实，白银货币化对中国古代商品经济的发展产生了深远影响。“银子”不仅是市场交易的主要流通媒介，更深刻塑造了城乡劳动力流动、雇佣报酬支付以及传统赋税征收的基本模式。 | Míng-Qīng yǐlái de jīngjìshǐ yánjiū zhèngshí, báiyín huòbìhuà duì Zhōngguó gǔdài shāngpǐn jīngjì de fāzhǎn chǎnshēng le shēnyuǎn yǐngxiǎng. "Yínzi" bùjǐn shì shìchǎng jiāoyì de zhǔyào liútōng méijiè, gèng shēnkè sùzào le chéng-xiāng láodònglì liúdòng, gùyòng bàochou zhīfù yǐjí chuántǒng fùshuì zhēngshōu de jīběn móshì. | Historical economic studies since the Ming and Qing dynasties confirm that silver monetization profoundly impacted ancient trade. Silver served not only as the primary medium of exchange, but shaped labor mobility, wages, and tax regimes. | Los estudios económicos confirman que la monetización de la plata desde las épocas Ming y Qing dinamizó el comercio. La plata sirvió de divisa principal y modeló la migración de mano de obra, los salarios y la recaudación fiscal.
